; claude: the educational applications (CATALOG.md's section): the
; programs made for a learner of a subject -- the sky, geometry, logic,
; typing -- rather than for getting work done. So far TinyStellarium
; (Stellarium, 2001), the planetarium, over appkits/astronomy, and
; TinyInteractivePhysics (Interactive Physics, 1989), the physics lab,
; over the Playground's Physics, its meters and its tape. Laid out
; like cad/: the programs here, software/ for the golden frames, web/
; for the browser.
;
; Not here: learning to program (TinyKarel and TinyCoreWar are games,
; games/programming/; Logo and Karel are ways, playground/ways/; Etoys
; is to be TinySqueak's, apps/devtools/), and the educational games
; (Oregon Trail, Carmen Sandiego, Number Munchers), which are played,
; so go by genre in games/.
;
; What else it might contain, each Tiny and after a famous original:
;  - PLATO (University of Illinois, 1960; TUTOR, 1967): lessons written
;    in TUTOR on the orange plasma screen, the first computer-based
;    teaching system, with libs/languages/tutor/ beside basic/;
;  - The Geometer's Sketchpad (1991) and Cabri Geometre (1988): a
;    construction that follows the point dragged, over appkits/sketch's
;    constraints and appkits/cad's crossings of lines and circles;
;  - Rocky's Boots (Warren Robinett, 1982): logic gates wired into
;    machines that sort the shapes going by;
;  - Mavis Beacon Teaches Typing (1987): lessons, speed and errors, over
;    libs/terminal's Vt;
;  - Kid Pix (Craig Hickman, 1989): painting with sounds, over
;    appkits/paint;
;  - Celestia (Chris Laurel, 2001): Stellarium's sky flown through in 3D,
;    over appkits/astronomy and the 3D playground;
;  - Encarta (Microsoft, 1993): an encyclopedia on a CD-ROM, articles,
;    pictures, sounds and links, over libs/web/.
